WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.344
Welcome to Grade 8 English, Unit 3: Community and Environment.

2
00:00:04.424 --> 00:00:12.336
In this unit you will explore how young people can make
a real difference in their communities by protecting the

3
00:00:12.416 --> 00:00:13.192
environment.

4
00:00:13.272 --> 00:00:19.899
You will read two information texts about
community action and about reading opinions closely,

5
00:00:19.979 --> 00:00:21.897
and the story "Rising Tide",

6
00:00:21.977 --> 00:00:30.317
about a girl named Imani who leads a youth movement called
Coastal Rise to clean up a polluted bay in a coastal Kenyan

7
00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:30.674
city.

8
00:00:30.754 --> 00:00:38.666
Along the way you will master 31 vocabulary words and
four grammar structures: clauses ending with prepositions,

9
00:00:38.746 --> 00:00:45.587
the second conditional, verb and adjective
preposition pairs, and the present continuous passive.

10
00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:52.009
You will also learn the formal language of
persuasion, such as "It is imperative that...",

11
00:00:52.089 --> 00:00:57.789
so that you can speak and write convincingly
about the issues that matter to you.

12
00:00:57.869 --> 00:01:03.783
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

13
00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.514
By the end of this unit,

14
00:01:05.594 --> 00:01:13.737
you will be able to read and understand a complex narrative
about community activism and environmental protection.

15
00:01:13.817 --> 00:01:19.291
You will also use 31 new vocabulary
words accurately in speaking and writing.

16
00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:25.278
You will also construct clauses that end
with prepositions naturally and correctly.

17
00:01:25.358 --> 00:01:27.947
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

18
00:01:28.027 --> 00:01:34.567
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: stifle,
wane, commemorate, articulate, hasten, advocate.

19
00:01:34.647 --> 00:01:39.824
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

20
00:01:39.904 --> 00:01:43.913
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

21
00:01:43.993 --> 00:01:50.194
The reading sequence includes When a Community
Decides to Act and Three Voices from the Harbour.

22
00:01:50.274 --> 00:01:51.110
Read actively.

23
00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:55.625
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

24
00:01:55.705 --> 00:01:59.878
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

25
00:01:59.958 --> 00:02:04.265
The first language focus is Clauses Ending with Prepositions.

26
00:02:04.345 --> 00:02:09.875
In natural English it is perfectly
correct to end a clause with a preposition:

27
00:02:09.955 --> 00:02:18.289
instead of the very formal "From which city did you come?",
a confident speaker asks "Which city did you come from?",

28
00:02:18.369 --> 00:02:21.381
and the sentence loses none of its meaning.

29
00:02:21.461 --> 00:02:29.220
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

30
00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:33.569
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Discussing the story.

31
00:02:33.649 --> 00:02:38.120
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

32
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.585
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

33
00:02:41.665 --> 00:02:45.186
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

34
00:02:45.266 --> 00:02:46.904
You are ready to begin.

35
00:02:46.984 --> 00:02:54.301
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

36
00:02:54.381 --> 00:02:57.887
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

37
00:02:57.967 --> 00:03:06.330
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
